A||||6||GeeDee86GT||Quick 2.5 Question||||5||
Z||000000||GeeDee86GT||02-04-2001||08:18 PM||||Are all 80's 2.5 engines the same? I can get a rebuilt S-10 unit and have an 84 which is really too nice to scrap.  Will it interchange?<BR>TIA<BR>Gary||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||02-05-2001||06:55 AM||||They should fit but you should check this site for anything about the Iron Duke...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/IronDuke.html" TARGET=_blank>www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/IronDuke.html</A> <P>As I recall there is a year break down link on the 4 cylinders. <P>Hope that helps.<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000002||Raydar||02-05-2001||10:12 AM||||Check Ogre's cave, too. (Link at the bottom of the page.) He's got some really good notes, too.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-05-2001||06:02 PM||||It might can be done but won't be easy. I looked at one awhile back there were several diferances.<P>The S10 starter is on the wrong side I think. You'll probably have to drill holes. There are other subtle diferances as well. In some years the S10 will need Fiero's EGR and maybe TBI put on it. S10 EGR is computer controlled in some years. I don't know what ones. I've only seen an 87 so far.<P>Also you'll have to use only the distributor version of the motor.<P>You'll also have to fool with the water pump and all that. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||02-05-2001||06:09 PM||||There are two different 2.5L 4's.  The Iron Duke and the Tech 4.  The Tech4 is an updated Duke with balance shafts to smooth out operation.  I'm not sure, but I think they are externally identical, so the swap should be a simple bolt in.<P>------------------<BR>We all come into this world the same way; naked, screaming, and covered in blood.  If you're lucky, it doesn't have to end there.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrossum||02-07-2001||03:05 PM||||s1- engine won't fit. fiero uses front wheel drive engine, and s-1- is rear whell driver. the engine mount bolt bosses are in the wrong spot as well as starter position. just about any 80-86 gm fwd 2.5 woll work, as long as you use your intake manifold, and your accessories..........||||reg||4
Z||000006||theogre||02-07-2001||07:03 PM||||F88 Tech4 means nothing. It is simply a lable stuck on to look important. Your distinction about tech 4 having the balance unit is incorrect. 87 has that label and is not a balancer motor. I think I've seen 85 and/or 86 also have that label on them. 85/86 are distributor motors.<P>The main issue is that the pre 86 cars won't take an 87 or later motor because of DIS ignition and the 700 series TBI. ||||reg||1
